  "intro": "With the prescription in his hand, Daniel goes to the pharmacy. To say 'I want to buy', Arabic joins the two verbs with أَنْ: أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَشْتَرِيَ (literally 'I want that I buy'). The second verb ends in -a after أَنْ. You also learn how to talk about doses: حَبَّة وَاحِدَة ثَلَاثَ مَرَّات فِي الْيَوْم (one tablet three times a day).",
